    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d362">

                <pb facs="0351" n="341" xml:id="pg341"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.796/164: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-08-23T14:00:00-04:00">August 23, 1941—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>566. Your 829, August 12, 9 p.m.<anchor n="39" xml:id="d362-f1"/> Harding<anchor
                        n="40" xml:id="d362-f2"/> has discussed Argentina’s commercial aviation
                    problems with Piñedo<anchor n="41" xml:id="d362-f3"/> and a memorandum of
                        conversation<anchor n="39" xml:id="d362-f4"/> is being forwarded to you by
                    airmail.</p>
                <p>It appears that Sana<anchor n="42" xml:id="d362-f5"/> and Corporatión<anchor
                        n="43" xml:id="d362-f6"/> will merge and that Aeroposta<anchor n="44"
                        xml:id="d362-f7"/> will be forced to join by reason of availability to the
                    merged organizations of up-to-date American equipment.</p>
                <p>It is understood that either Wilcox or Oscar Muller will be authorized to handle
                    the financial arrangements on behalf of the Federal Loan Agency and that Piñedo
                    will assist in effecting the merger.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d362-f1" n="39" xml:id="d362-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d362-f2" n="40" xml:id="d362-f2-content">
                <p>William Barclay Harding, vice president of the Defense Supplies Corporatión, a
                    buying agency of the Federal Loan Agency.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d362-f3" n="41" xml:id="d362-f3-content">
                <p>Federico Piñedo, formerly Argentine Minister of Finance.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d362-f4" n="39" xml:id="d362-f4-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d362-f5" n="42" xml:id="d362-f5-content">
                <p>Sociedad Argentina de Navegación Aérea.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d362-f6" n="43" xml:id="d362-f6-content">
                <p>Corporación Sudamericana de Servicios Aéreos.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d362-f7" n="44" xml:id="d362-f7-content">
                <p>Aeroposta Argentina.</p>
            </note>
